WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.029
<v Examiner>Two marks.

2
00:00:02.029 --> 00:00:06.978
<v Examiner>Describe the function of the placental barrier, and define a teratogenic effect.

3
00:00:07.428 --> 00:00:09.091
Her formative two answers.

4
00:00:09.091 --> 00:00:13.889
The placental barrier separates the mother's blood from the foetus's blood.

5
00:00:13.889 --> 00:00:19.647
It's a non-selective barrier: many nutrients and molecules, including drugs, can cross it.

6
00:00:19.647 --> 00:00:25.213
A teratogenic effect is the effect of a substance, like a medicine, alcohol or a virus,

7
00:00:25.213 --> 00:00:28.988
that alters the development of the foetus during pregnancy,

8
00:00:28.988 --> 00:00:33.978
for example the growth and development of the brain, leading to abnormalities.

9
00:00:33.978 --> 00:00:37.240
The first trimester is the time of greatest danger.

10
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.991
Her deck's historic example is thalidomide.

11
00:00:40.441 --> 00:00:43.072
The rest of the lifespan in a line each.

12
00:00:43.072 --> 00:00:47.872
Breastfeeding: drugs pass into breastmilk, so weigh risk against benefit.

13
00:00:47.872 --> 00:00:53.264
Children: their liver and kidneys are immature, so doses are worked out by weight.

14
00:00:53.264 --> 00:00:57.341
And to get a toddler to take a medicine, offer simple choices,

15
00:00:57.341 --> 00:00:59.182
like the syringe or the cup.

16
00:00:59.182 --> 00:01:01.878
Never hide it in food or call it a lolly.

17
00:01:01.878 --> 00:01:07.533
Older adults: decreased renal function and slower liver metabolism, so drugs build up.

18
00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:12.859
They're often on many medicines, which is polypharmacy, so start low and go slow,

19
00:01:12.859 --> 00:01:14.306
and use blister packs.

20
00:01:14.756 --> 00:01:20.333
Placental barrier: separates maternal and foetal blood, non-selective, drugs cross.

21
00:01:20.333 --> 00:01:24.970
Teratogenic: alters foetal development, worst in the first trimester.

22
00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:30.278
Children: immature liver and kidneys, weight-based doses, offer simple choices.

23
00:01:30.278 --> 00:01:35.385
Older adults: decreased renal function, polypharmacy, start low and go slow.
